{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01U2", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fppf-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f00758df3c4070f559b8a5354de1d8c282b25aa28e638b2802fcab98be0a9d87", "source_text": "A flat morphism locally of finite presentation is universally open.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f84ddab678262b4e472730a6cb98f1b3051792337dd22c621cf28bc54682a941", "unit_id": "tag:01UA:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01U2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0007": "$U_i \\to S$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$U_i \\subset X$", "MATH_0010": "$U_i$", "MATH_0011": "$V_i \\subset S$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}_S(V_i) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0013": "$U_i \\to V_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-generalizations-lift-flat}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-locally-finite-presentation-universally-open}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-flat}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-finite-presentation}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-flat-characterize}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-locally-finite-presentation-characterize}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{algebra-proposition-fppf-open}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dcb481da178626a1a6e292bb24e7a5d2a9dd6b4acf9003cba5be625e533f2594", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:60f7c5a27abc8a681b97d87d9e9dfe2a7e4145ceb0f973137b5b6411b0720b4f", "source_text": "This follows from Lemmas <REF_0001> and\nLemma <REF_0002> above.\nWe can also argue directly as follows.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nLet <MATH_0001> be flat and locally of finite presentation.\nBy Lemmas <REF_0003> and\n<REF_0004> any base change of <MATH_0002> is flat\nand locally of finite presentation. Hence it suffices to show <MATH_0003> is open.\nTo show <MATH_0004> is open it suffices to show that we may cover\n<MATH_0005> by open affines <MATH_0006> such that <MATH_0007>\nis open. We may cover <MATH_0008> by affine opens <MATH_0009> such that each\n<MATH_0010> maps into an affine open <MATH_0011> and such that\nthe induced ring map <MATH_0012> is\nflat and of finite presentation (Lemmas <REF_0005> and\n<REF_0006>).\nThen <MATH_0013> is open by\nAlgebra, Proposition <REF_0007>\nand the proof is complete.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c345d5216250308467116bddc5f77445820503c19cdf374499a89f35ffbfcc45", "unit_id": "tag:01UA:proof"}
